<In_August_1815_Austen_began_work_on_her_last_complete_novel,_'Persuasion',_which_she_finished_in_August_1816,_the_year_in_which_a_second_edition_of_'Mansfield_Park'_was_published_(like_'Emma',_by_Byron's_publisher,_John_Murray).> <base.kwebbase.kwsentence.previous_sentence> "Generally regarded as her greatest achievement, 'Emma' is the work which most fully realized Austen's own criterion of  \'three or four families in a country village\' as \'the very thing to work on,\'  and received a favourable review in March 1816 'Quarterly Review' from Sir Walter Scott, who hailed this \'nameless author\' as a masterful exponent of \'the modern novel\' in the new realist tradition." .
