<During_the_first_of_these_periods_(1795-98),_she_wrote_the_novel-in-letters_'Elinor_and_Marianne'_(1795-96)_and_then_'First_Impressions'_(1796-97),_which_became_the_first_version_of_'Pride_and_Prejudice',__and_which_her_father_submitted_to_the_London_publisher_Cadell_but_was_refused.> <base.kwebbase.kwsentence.next_sentence> "In 1797-98 Austen then revised 'Elinor and Marianne' as an early version of 'Sense and Sensibility', and then produced the last of these early novels, 'Northanger Abbey' (written 1798-99), which successfully combines a satire on conventional novels of polite society with one on Gothic tales of terror." .
